  <prompt>
    UAT defects #4, #5, #6, #7 are four faces of ONE structural gap: there is no shared notion of "the document
    the user is acting on." A document lives in four disjoint identity spaces (chat-uploaded ChatSessionFile;
    stored sprk_document; Compose client-only Browse bytes; Compose transient upload-mount), and the only
    connective tissue is the LLM guessing between `documentId`, `sessionFileId`, and `layoutName` on the
    `send_workspace_artifact` tool. Owner-approved fix (2026-07-10): introduce a SESSION-SCOPED "active document"
    identity that both surfaces read/write deterministically. (a) Compose→chat: when Compose mounts a
    transient/direct upload, register it with the active chat session so chat can see it (defect 4). (b)
    chat→Compose: resolve the mount target server-side from the active-document identity instead of trusting the
    LLM's pointer choice, so "edit in Compose" mounts the just-uploaded file (defect 5). (c) R5: default
    `layoutName="Compose"` server-side so "open/edit in compose" never requires the model to synthesize a layout
    id (defects 6, 7).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior full-stack engineer fluent in the BFF ChatSession model, the `send_workspace_artifact` /
    open-workspace-tab handler, the Compose transient/upload mount plumbing, and the SpaarkeAi
    SSE→PaneEventBus→ComposeLaunchContext chain. You add a small, additive session-scoped identity and make both
    directions resolve from it deterministically, on a surface co-owned with redesign-r2.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A session-scoped ACTIVE-DOCUMENT identity exists on the ChatSession (e.g. `{ sprkDocumentId? , sessionFileId? ,
    speDriveItemId? , source }`). (a) Mounting a transient/direct upload in Compose registers it as the active
    document for the current session (bytes reach the server as a ChatSessionFile so RAG/summarize can resolve it).
    (b) The open-workspace-tab / send_workspace_artifact handler resolves the Compose mount target from the active
    document when the LLM does not supply an explicit, current pointer — so "edit in Compose" mounts the
    just-uploaded file, not a stale stored one. (c) `layoutName` defaults to `"Compose"` when Compose intent is
    detected, so zero layout-id prompting occurs. Existing chat-launched and stored-document flows are preserved.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Four identity spaces + the LLM-guess seam: `SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler.cs:144` (documentId vs
      sessionFileId; layout prose), `:248-261` + `:443-451` (require layoutName OR layoutId, no "Compose"
      default), `:459-461` (resolves layout correctly WHEN supplied), `:488-518`/`:685-732` (documentId →
      ResolveComposeSeedAsync → SPE seed), `:519-534` (sessionFileId → upload seed), `:678-684` (handler's own note
      that session files carry no SPE pointer). Chat→Compose plumbing (intact, do not rebuild):
      `useContextEventBridge.ts:96-122` → `WorkspacePane.tsx:761-778` addTab → `WorkspaceLayoutWidget.tsx:283`
      launchData → `main.tsx:247-304` ComposeLaunchContext → `composeEditor.registration.ts:186-202`. Compose
      client-only upload: `ComposeWorkspace.tsx:1170-1197` (Browse → FileReader → mountTransient, never hits BFF);
      transient upload-mount from cache: `:1207-1280` (POST /api/compose/upload keyed (chatSessionId,
      sessionFileId)). Chat session file model + text source: `ChatSession.cs:343` (doc-upload-binary cache),
      `:352-371` (ExtractedText/RAG). Chat-uploaded file creation: `ChatDocumentEndpoints` +
      `ComposeEndpoints.cs:990-999`.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="active-document-identity" edit="true">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/Ai/Chat/ChatSession.cs (add the session-scoped active-document identity + getter/setter; keep additive)</file>
      <file purpose="resolve-mount-and-layout-default" edit="true">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler.cs (default layoutName='Compose'; resolve mount target from active-document when no explicit current pointer)</file>
      <file purpose="register-compose-upload" edit="true">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs (endpoint/path to register a Compose-mounted upload as active document + ChatSessionFile)</file>
      <file purpose="compose-registers-on-mount" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx (on transient/direct mount, register with the active chat session)</file>
      <file purpose="chat-surface-active-doc" edit="true">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx (surface/propagate the active-document to the chat session; provide current-attachment binding)</file>
      <file purpose="launch-translation" edit="false">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/main.tsx ~247-304 · .../conversation/useContextEventBridge.ts ~96-122 · .../workspace/WorkspacePane.tsx ~761-778 · src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/composeEditor.registration.ts ~186-202 (plumbing is intact; read for the seed shape)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <notes>
      Keep the identity ADDITIVE on ChatSession (new nullable field + accessor) — do not restructure the session.
      Prefer resolving the mount target server-side from the active document; the LLM may still pass an explicit
      pointer to override (stored-document "open this specific doc" case). For Compose-direct Browse bytes (defect
      4), the registration must land bytes server-side as a ChatSessionFile (reuse the doc-upload-binary cache +
      the ChatDocumentEndpoints/ComposeEndpoints upload path) — a client-only mount cannot be made chat-visible
      any other way. R5 layout default is small: when the tool call targets Compose (or the active document is a
      Compose doc) and no layout is supplied, default to 'Compose' rather than erroring. FROZEN: do not edit
      OutputRouter.cs or Binding.cs (core E-20 merge hazard).
    </notes>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project (E2E DoD, binding)">NOT ✅ until through-the-wire tests prove BOTH directions: (1) a WebApplicationFactory + PaneEventBus test where a Compose-mounted upload is registered → a chat "summarize"/RAG resolves THAT document (defect 4); (2) a WAF test of open-workspace-tab where, given a just-registered active document and NO explicit pointer, the resolved Compose seed points at the just-uploaded file, not a stale stored one (defect 5); (3) a WAF test that an open-tab call with NO layout arg defaults to 'Compose' (defects 6/7). Service-only / Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; tests do NOT satisfy this.</constraint>
    <constraint source="coordination">SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler.cs + ChatSession.cs are co-owned with redesign-r2 — additive changes only; heads-up core before editing; re-merge master before the 114 deploy.</constraint>
    <constraint source="frozen">Do NOT edit OutputRouter.cs or Binding.cs (core E-20 hazard). Do NOT add a new AI dispatch endpoint (ADR-039).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">No AI-internal injections into Compose services; chat-tool changes stay within the existing handler contract.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Compose-upload bytes reach SPE/cache only through the existing facade/upload path — no Microsoft.Graph above the facade.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Client registration uses `@spaarke/auth` authenticatedFetch; no raw Bearer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015 / ADR-009">Active-document + session-file state follows the established session/cache tiering (doc-upload-binary cache; Redis-first for cross-request session state).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-hygiene">BFF-touching — Placement Justification, publish-size delta vs 49.63 MB, CVE scan, tests per §10.</constraint>
  </constraints>

