  <justification component="Session-scoped active-document identity (additive to ChatSession)">
    <existing>ChatSession, ChatSessionFile, the doc-upload-binary cache, ResolveComposeSeedAsync, and the SSE→ComposeLaunchContext plumbing all exist; what is missing is a shared "which document is active" fact.</existing>
    <extension>Add one additive nullable identity on ChatSession + make the existing handler resolve from it and default the layout; register Compose uploads through the existing upload/cache path. No new dispatch endpoint, no new session model, no parallel document store (per CLAUDE.md §11 — extend, don't duplicate).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it: chat cannot see Compose-uploaded documents (defect 4), "edit in Compose" mounts the wrong/stale file (defect 5), and "open in compose" dead-ends asking for a layout id (defects 6/7) — the entire Assistant↔Compose collaboration the owner tested is broken.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load the triage note + tasks 010/012/070 + ADR-030/039 + bff-extensions.md. State Placement Justification. Heads-up core (coordination note) before editing the co-owned files. Read the handler seam + the mount plumbing + ChatSession file model.</step>
    <step order="1">Add the additive session-scoped active-document identity to ChatSession (nullable field + accessor). Define its source discriminant (stored / session-upload / compose-direct).</step>
    <step order="2">R5 (small): in SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler, default `layoutName='Compose'` when Compose intent is present and no layout is supplied; remove the requirement that forces the model to synthesize a layout id.</step>
    <step order="3">chat→Compose (defect 5): resolve the Compose mount seed from the active document when the LLM supplies no explicit current pointer; keep explicit-pointer override for stored-document "open this specific doc".</step>
    <step order="4">Compose→chat (defect 4): on a transient/direct Compose mount, register the document as active AND land its bytes server-side as a ChatSessionFile (reuse the doc-upload-binary cache + existing upload path) so summarize/RAG resolves it. Wire ConversationPane to propagate the current-attachment binding.</step>
    <step order="5">Add the three through-the-wire tests (WAF + PaneEventBus) named in the E2E DoD constraint (defect-4 resolve, defect-5 correct mount, defect-6/7 layout default). Build BFF + affected client packages; measure publish-size delta; CVE scan; NetArchTest facade green.</step>
    <step order="6">code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5). Update TASK-INDEX + current-task.md. Confirm no edits to OutputRouter.cs/Binding.cs.</step>
  </steps>

